        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Full Theorem1.2 and Section2.1–2.3 author construction are supplied, including all new coordinate/mean-curvature estimates, the replacement metric and the collar scalar-curvature margin. n>=3, the initial quotient is the standard parabolic lattice translation quotient, and the conclusion is existence of a complete non-globally-hyperbolic Riemannian manifold isometric to that quotient outside compact subsets with R>=-n(n-1). The statement does not assert a fixed topology or a global metric perturbation on the same manifold; those later refinements are not counted. The published corner-smoothing theorem [8,Theorem5] and standard warped scalar-curvature formula are background, while their applicability and absorption of the epsilon loss are explicitly proved. Lemma2.1 coordinate derivatives are author-marked routine computations, not a missing new core."
      },
